{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_TCPIP_SECTION_6_Requirements_Tracing","src":"manifest","doc":"SWS_TcpIp","page":24,"text":"6 Requirements Tracing\nThe following tables reference the requirements specified in Chapter 3 and links to the\nfulfillment of these. Please note that if column “Satisfied by” is empty for a specific\nrequirement this means that this requirement is not fulfilled by this document.\nRequirement\nDescription\nSatisfied by\n[RS_IPSEC_00004]\nThe Internet Key Exchange (IKEv2)\nProtocol shall be supported\naccording to IETF RFC 7296\n[SWS_TcpIp_00353]\n[RS_IPSEC_00010]\nIKEv2 shall support periodic\nreauthentication and rekeying\n[SWS_TcpIp_00355]\n[RS_IPSEC_00011]\nIKEv2 shall support a seamless\nhandover of exchanged keys\n[SWS_TcpIp_00355]\n[RS_IPSEC_00013]\nIKEv2 shall support dead peer\ndetection\n[SWS_TcpIp_00355]\n[RS_IPSEC_00014]\nIKEv2 shall support authentication\nbased on X.509v3 certificates with\ndigital signatures\n[SWS_TcpIp_00356]\n[RS_IPSEC_00021]\nAll algorithms which are classified as\n\"MUST\" in IETF RFC 8247 shall be\nsupported by IKEv2\n[SWS_TcpIp_00353]\n[RS_IPSEC_00022]\nIPsec’s Security Policy Database\n(SPD) shall be configurable for IPs,\nIP ranges, protocols, ports and port\nranges\n[SWS_TcpIp_00357]\n[RS_IPSEC_00023]\nIPsec’s Security Policy Database\n(SPD) default behavior shall be\nBYPASS\n[SWS_TcpIp_00357]\n[RS_IPSEC_00025]\nIPsec’s Peer Authorization Database\n(PAD) shall be configurable for use\nwith X.509v3\n[SWS_TcpIp_00356]\n[RS_IPSEC_00027]\nIt shall be possible to define the\npriority order of the algorithms used\nby IKEv2 during the IKE_INIT\nnegotiations\n[SWS_TcpIp_00358]\n[RS_Ids_00810]\nBasic SW security events\n[SWS_TcpIp_00361] [SWS_TcpIp_00362]\n[SWS_TcpIp_00382] [SWS_TcpIp_00383]\n[SWS_TcpIp_00384] [SWS_TcpIp_00385]\n[SWS_TcpIp_00386] [SWS_TcpIp_00387]\n[SWS_TcpIp_00388] [SWS_TcpIp_00389]\n[SWS_TcpIp_00394] [SWS_TcpIp_00395]\n[SWS_TcpIp_00396] [SWS_TcpIp_00422]\n[SWS_TcpIp_00423] [SWS_TcpIp_00424]\n[SWS_TcpIp_00425] [SWS_TcpIp_00426]\n[SRS_BSW_00323]\nAll AUTOSAR Basic Software\nModules shall check passed API\nparameters for validity\n[SWS_TcpIp_00147]\n[SRS_BSW_00452]\nClassification of runtime…","caption":"6 Requirements Tracing","sha":null,"series":[{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_TCPIP_SECTION_6_Requirements_Tracing","releases":["R23-11"],"page":21,"hash":"83d5b8b8e7a77dcb","caption":"","screenshot_path":"_src/spec/snippets/assets/0c56201f2483/page_21.webp"},{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_TCPIP_SECTION_6_Requirements_Tracing","releases":["R24-11"],"page":24,"hash":"ed8fe89de987a3f4","caption":"","screenshot_path":"_src/spec/snippets/assets/516461f0639e/page_24.webp"},{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_TCPIP_SECTION_6_Requirements_Tracing","releases":["R25-11"],"page":25,"hash":"2eb7c90173d42e51","caption":"","screenshot_path":"_src/spec/snippets/assets/2f3168688501/page_25.webp"}],"releases":["R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"screenshot_path":"_src/spec/snippets/assets/2f3168688501/page_25.webp","trel":"R25-11","tstat":"section","kind":"snippet","platform":"classic","targets":[{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.98,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"","why":"Explizite Erwähnung von SWS_TCPIP_00020 im Text des Dokuments AUTOSAR_CP_SWS_TcpIp.pdf.","rel":["R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"id":"SWS_TCPIP_00020"},{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.98,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"","why":"Explizite Erwähnung von SWS_TCPIP_00040 im Text des Dokuments AUTOSAR_CP_SWS_TcpIp.pdf.","rel":["R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"id":"SWS_TCPIP_00040"},{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.98,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"","why":"Explizite Erwähnung von SWS_TCPIP_00189 im Text des Dokuments AUTOSAR_CP_SWS_TcpIp.pdf.","rel":["R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"id":"SWS_TCPIP_00189"},{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.98,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"","why":"Explizite Erwähnung von SWS_TCPIP_00190 im Text des Dokuments AUTOSAR_CP_SWS_TcpIp.pdf.","rel":["R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"id":"SWS_TCPIP_00190"},{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.98,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","